        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f41d04ed-bfdb-5ad9-9611-7b44a31d5f3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horton Foote, David Foster Wallace, Thomas C. Ryan, Katya Alpert Gilden, Bert Gilden, K.B. Gilden, Otto Preminger\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird, Tender Mercies, Hurry Sundown, Between the Hills and the Sea\n- Topics: screenwriting, playwriting, television drama, novels, film adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was born on March 14, 1916, and died on March 4, 2009.\n- Horton Foote was an American playwright and screenwriter.\n- Horton Foote was known for the screenplays for the 1962 film \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" and the 1983 film \"Tender Mercies,\" and for live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\n- David Foster Wallace was born on February 21, 1962, and died on September 12, 2008.\n- David Foster Wallace was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing.\n- Katya Alpert Gilden and Bert Gilden used the pseudonym K.B. Gilden.\n- Katya Alpert Gilden and Bert Gilden produced the novel \"Hurry Sundown\" in 1964.\n- Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan wrote the screenplay for the film \"Hurry Sundown,\" based on the 1965 novel of the same title by K.B. Gilden.\n- Otto Preminger made \"Hurry Sundown\" into a film in 1967.\n- Katya Alpert Gilden and Bert Gilden produced the novel \"Between the Hills and the Sea\" in 1971, and it was published four months after Bert Gilden's death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6b8f6514-c2c9-5798-8f97-04233421a68e",
        "text": "Page: Horton Foote. Sentence: Albert Horton Foote Jr. (March 14, 1916March 4, 2009) was an American playwright and screenwriter, perhaps best known for his screenplays for the 1962 film \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" and the 1983 film \"Tender Mercies\", and his notable live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\nPage: David Foster Wallace. Sentence: David Foster Wallace (February 21, 1962 – September 12, 2008) was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing.\nPage: Hurry Sundown (film). Sentence: The screenplay by Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan is based on the 1965 novel of the same title by K.B. Gilden, a pseudonym for married couple Katya and Bert Gilden.\nPage: Katya Alpert Gilden. Sentence: The couple produced two major novels, \"Hurry Sundown\" (1964), which was made into an Otto Preminger film in 1967, and \"Between the Hills and the Sea\" (1971), published four months after Bert's death.",
